# SA-EP-003 — Enterprise Service Relationships

**Project:** BTA V5.1 — HCGO Enterprise Service Architecture

**Status:** Approved

**Classification:** Enterprise Service Architecture

---

# Purpose

Establish the authoritative architectural relationships between Enterprise Services across HCGO.

Enterprise Service Relationships faithfully represent approved Enterprise Capability Relationships while preserving enterprise authority, ownership, stewardship, governance, lifecycle authority, traceability, enterprise boundaries, and enterprise semantics.

Enterprise Service Relationships are architectural constructs.

They are not runtime execution.

They are not orchestration.

They are not APIs.

They are not implementation dependencies.

---

# Architecture Objective

Establish the authoritative architectural relationships between Enterprise Services across HCGO.

Enterprise Service Relationships faithfully represent Enterprise Capability Relationships while preserving enterprise authority and enterprise semantics.

Enterprise Service Relationships remain:

- Enterprise-level
- Technology independent
- Domain independent
- Implementation independent
- Runtime independent

---

# Enterprise Service Relationship Principles

Enterprise Service Relationships shall identify architectural relationships only.

Enterprise Service Relationships shall preserve:

- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Traceability
- Enterprise Information Boundaries
- Enterprise Capability Boundaries
- Enterprise Service Boundaries

Enterprise Service Relationships shall never imply:

- Runtime sequencing
- Service invocation
- REST APIs
- HTTP communication
- Messaging
- Event processing
- Database relationships
- Implementation dependencies
- Technology implementation

Those responsibilities belong to the Technology Implementation phase.

---

# Enterprise Service Relationship Model

For every Enterprise Service identify:

- Enterprise Service
- Authoritative Enterprise Capability
- Related Enterprise Services
- Relationship Purpose
- Relationship Classification
- Relationship Boundaries
- Relationship Constraints
- Governance Notes

Relationship classifications may include:

- Provider → Consumer
- Architectural Dependency
- Governance Relationship
- Stewardship Relationship
- Information Relationship
- Traceability Relationship
- Future approved enterprise relationship classifications

These classifications describe enterprise architecture.

They do not describe runtime behavior.

---

# Enterprise Principle

Enterprise Service Relationships faithfully represent Enterprise Capability Relationships.

Enterprise Service Relationships expose architectural collaboration between Enterprise Services.

Enterprise Service Relationships shall never redefine:

- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Capability Relationships
- Enterprise Semantics

Enterprise Service Relationships remain architectural representations of Enterprise Capability Relationships.

---

# Constitutional Relationship Preservation

Enterprise Service Relationships shall faithfully represent approved Enterprise Capability Relationships.

Enterprise Service Relationships shall never create, redefine, replace, or override Enterprise Capability Relationships.

Enterprise authority, ownership, stewardship, governance, lifecycle authority, traceability, enterprise boundaries, and enterprise semantics remain vested in the owning Enterprise Capabilities.

Enterprise Service Relationships expose architectural collaboration between Enterprise Services while preserving the authority of the Enterprise Capabilities they represent.

---

# Architectural Rationale

This preserves the constitutional separation between:

- Enterprise Capability
- Enterprise Capability Relationship
- Enterprise Service
- Enterprise Service Relationship
- Technology Implementation

Each architectural layer has a distinct constitutional responsibility.

Enterprise Capability Relationships define how enterprise responsibilities relate.

Enterprise Service Relationships define how the services exposing those responsibilities relate architecturally.

Technology implements those relationships without redefining them.

---

# Constitutional Principle

Enterprise Capability Relationships define authoritative enterprise responsibility relationships.

Enterprise Service Relationships faithfully represent those approved Enterprise Capability Relationships.

Technology faithfully implements Enterprise Service Relationships.

Neither architectural representation nor technology implementation may redefine:

- Enterprise Capability Relationships
- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Traceability
- Enterprise Boundaries
- Enterprise Semantics

---

# Architecture Outcome

Enterprise Service Relationships become the authoritative architectural relationship model for Enterprise Services across HCGO.

Every Enterprise Service Relationship shall trace directly to an approved Enterprise Capability Relationship.

Technology implementations shall faithfully implement Enterprise Service Relationships without redefining:

- Enterprise Capabilities
- Enterprise Capability Relationships
- Enterprise Services
- Enterprise Authority
- Enterprise Ownership
- Enterprise Stewardship
- Enterprise Governance
- Enterprise Lifecycle Authority
- Enterprise Traceability
- Enterprise Boundaries
- Enterprise Semantics

Enterprise Service Relationships therefore become the authoritative architectural bridge between the Enterprise Service Catalog and Technology Implementation.

---

# Current Assessment

Enterprise Service Architecture consists of three complementary architectural artifacts:

- SA-EP-001 — Enterprise Service Architecture Principles
- SA-EP-002 — Enterprise Service Catalog
- SA-EP-003 — Enterprise Service Relationships

Together these artifacts establish:

- The constitutional principles governing Enterprise Services.
- The authoritative inventory of Enterprise Services.
- The authoritative architectural relationships between Enterprise Services.

They remain:

- Enterprise-level
- Technology independent
- Domain independent
- Implementation independent
- Runtime independent

They do not define runtime execution, orchestration, APIs, messaging, persistence implementation, or technology implementation.

Those responsibilities begin with the Technology Implementation phase.

This preserves the foundational HCGO constitutional principles:

- Enterprise Service Architecture faithfully represents Enterprise Capability Architecture.
- Enterprise Service Relationships faithfully represent Enterprise Capability Relationships.
- Technology Implementation faithfully implements Enterprise Service Architecture.

Neither architectural representation nor technology implementation may redefine enterprise authority, enterprise ownership, enterprise stewardship, enterprise governance, enterprise lifecycle authority, enterprise boundaries, enterprise relationships, or enterprise semantics established through earlier architectural phases.